                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>Undo history holds up to 50 steps of node + link snapshots.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- 15. AI Assistant -->
        <section id="ai-assistant" class="docs-section">
          <h2>15. AI Assistant</h2>
          <p>
            The chat panel (toolbar chat icon) is an AI <b>modelling copilot</b>. By default it
            uses <b>EPANetLab free (hosted)</b> mode: no key required — messages are routed through
            a small server-side proxy holding a shared app-level Gemini key, with a limited daily
            quota. You can also bring your own key with any other provider.
          </p>
          <h3>Providers</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><b>EPANetLab free (hosted)</b> — default; no key required.</li>
            <li><b>Google Gemini (free tier)</b> — free key from AI Studio.</li>
            <li><b>OpenRouter (free models)</b> — auto-selects a current free model.</li>
            <li><b>Ollama (local, no key)</b> — run models on your machine.</li>
            <li><b>LM Studio (local, no key)</b></li>
            <li><b>OpenAI (paid)</b></li>
            <li><b>Anthropic Claude (paid)</b></li>
            <li><b>Custom OpenAI-compatible</b> — any endpoint (vLLM, LiteLLM, Together, DeepSeek…)</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>What it can do</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Summarize the current model and its simulation status.</li>
            <li>Build a network (add junctions, tanks, reservoirs, pipes, pumps, valves).</li>
            <li>Edit or delete elements and set properties.</li>
            <li>Run the simulation and interpret results (e.g. "which nodes have low pressure?").</li>
            <li>Run spatial queries against your synced network (elements within a radius, network length within a region).</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Try the four example prompts shown in the empty chat. The chat digests the current model
            automatically, so answers stay grounded in your actual network.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 16. Privacy -->
        <section id="privacy" class="docs-section">
          <h2>16. Privacy</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>The app is <b>private and not open source</b>; the repository is not distributed.</li>
            <li>Drawing, simulation, and saving happen on your device. Autosave and named projects stay in browser storage.</li>
            <li>Basic page-usage analytics (Google Analytics) collect only visit statistics for the site owner; no model data is transmitted.</li>
            <li>Optional email sign-in (magic-link, no password) enables cloud sync via Supabase.</li>
            <li>In EPANetLab free (hosted) chat mode, messages pass through a minimal proxy with a shared app-level key; no personal key is used. With any other provider, keys never leave your browser.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- 17. FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="docs-section">
          <h2>17. FAQ & Troubleshooting</h2>
          <dl class="doc-faq">
            <dt>The simulation won't run.</dt>
            <dd>You need at least one reservoir or tank and at least one pipe. An alert appears if either is missing.</dd>
            <dt>"Simulation completed with warnings."</dt>
            <dd>Check the results panel and inspect low-pressure nodes (red) or high velocities. The solver report text is captured internally.</dd>
            <dt>My imported drawing is in the wrong place.</dt>
            <dd>Un-projected files cannot be positioned automatically — use the Positioning dialog (UTM zone / hemisphere / units) or "Use current map location", then drag on the map.</dd>
            <dt>Where did my project go?</dt>
            <dd>Autosave restores your last working session. Named projects are under Load; cloud copies appear there too when signed in.</dd>
            <dt>How do I label nodes in AutoCAD?</dt>
            <dd>Export node positions CSV, or export a DXF (<code>DXFOUT</code> / Export CAD button): it carries annotation text (diameter, length, elevation…) on separate <code>ANN.*</code> layers you can style or freeze.</dd>
            <dt>Can I share the layout with Google Earth?</dt>
            <dd>Yes — <code>KMLOUT</code> / <code>KMZOUT</code> (or Export KML) writes every node and pipe as a placemark with label text and themed colors.</dd>
            <dt>Can I import an .inp file?</dt>
            <dd>Not yet — export is supported; import is planned.</dd>
            <dt>Why is pressure shown in meters rather than psi?</dt>
            <dd>Result units follow the View tab unit system (SI vs US).</dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

